That, I think, is the actual killer version: Arena.ai for internet identity, where “winning” means a domain causes the right actors to understand and successfully use the product—not merely that somebody thinks it sounds cool.

And it gives name.com something strategically useful: a potential recommend_domain(intent, audience, constraints) intelligence layer that could sit in front of their API for AI builders and partners, while naturally driving every successful recommendation into name.com registration. Their hackathon rubric explicitly rewards central, multi-endpoint, unexpected API applications, which this fits extremely closely.

